---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'What exactly does OriginsLynk do?',
    answer: 'OriginsLynk studies repetitive business work, identifies the steps a dependable system can handle, and builds that system around the way you already operate. Common examples include preparing follow-up, organizing incoming requests, drafting recurring reports, routing exceptions, and keeping routine handoffs visible.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Which service is right for me?',
    answer: 'Choose the Automation Health Check when an existing automation is unreliable or unclear. Choose Tier 1 for two client-started workflows, Tier 2 for four total workflows including two scheduled or supported connected workflows, or Tier 3 for six total workflows in a dedicated environment OriginsLynk maintains. A fit call confirms the recommendation before a proposal.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What is included in the $350 Automation Health Check?',
    answer: 'The starting scope covers up to three existing workflows on one automation platform, a discovery and screen-share session, safe non-destructive testing when possible, review of failures, access, duplicate tools, subscriptions, and data risk, written findings, a prioritized action plan, and a results meeting. Repairs are separate.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Why are specific software providers not listed?',
    answer: 'OriginsLynk selects and configures appropriate third-party software and AI services according to each project’s compatibility, security, and workflow requirements. Required client-owned subscriptions and data-processing providers are disclosed during proposal and onboarding.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What subscriptions will I need?',
    answer: 'That depends on the agreed workflows and accounts you already use. Required subscriptions, provider charges, message fees, storage fees, and usage-based costs are disclosed before onboarding and are paid by the client unless the written proposal says otherwise.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Who owns the Tier 3 appliance?',
    answer: 'OriginsLynk owns the appliance and rents it as part of the managed service. The appliance is dedicated to one client and must be returned when managed service ends.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Does the Tier 3 appliance remain at my location?',
    answer: 'Yes, during the managed service. The dedicated small computer is placed at the client’s site. The client provides power, internet connectivity, and reasonable physical access while OriginsLynk remotely administers the agreed environment.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Who owns my accounts and business data?',
    answer: 'You retain ownership of your accounts, subscriptions, client-provided business data, and business outputs. OriginsLynk retains its reusable methods and generalized implementation patterns without claiming ownership of your source information.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Can I revoke account access?',
    answer: 'Yes. Client-controlled account authorization is preferred so you can revoke access from the account itself. Credentials and authorization are handled through the approved onboarding process, never through the public consultation form or ordinary email.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Will the system send messages or change records automatically?',
    answer: 'Consequential messages, record changes, and business actions remain human-approved unless a specific workflow authorization establishes a different review process in writing. Low-risk automation boundaries are documented and tested before production use.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What happens when an integration stops working?',
    answer: 'OriginsLynk investigates detected failures during the support period or managed-care hours in the service agreement. A provider outage, changed authorization, account restriction, or changed feature may require the client or provider to resolve its portion, and replacement work may be quoted separately.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Are AI-generated outputs always correct?',
    answer: 'No. AI-generated content and decisions may be incomplete or incorrect. Clients remain responsible for reviewing outputs and approving consequential business actions unless a written workflow authorization establishes a different review process.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What does the monthly care plan include?',
    answer: 'The $250 monthly plan includes appliance rental, automated monitoring, backup verification, routine maintenance, failure investigation, a monthly service report, business-hours support, and up to 30 minutes of minor workflow adjustments.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What is excluded from the monthly plan?',
    answer: 'It excludes new workflows, new integrations, major workflow changes, vendor migrations, custom development, after-hours emergency response, guaranteed uptime, third-party subscriptions, and usage-based charges.',
  },
  {
    question: 'What happens when I cancel?',
    answer: 'OriginsLynk removes managed access and credentials, provides available exports described in the service agreement, follows the agreed data-retention and offboarding process, and arranges return of the OriginsLynk-owned appliance. Client-owned accounts remain with the client.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Are regulated or high-risk workflows supported?',
    answer: 'They are excluded by default. Work involving regulated information or consequential medical, legal, credit, employment, insurance, or financial decisions requires explicit written approval, appropriate safeguards, and separate scope. OriginsLynk may decline the work.',
  },
  {
    question: 'How are additional workflows priced?',
    answer: 'Additional templated workflows start at $300 only when they use the existing environment and supported integrations, follow an established OriginsLynk pattern, require no major custom development, and take about two to three implementation hours. New, complex, unsupported, or high-risk work is quoted separately.',
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="Frequently asked questions"
  description="Answers about OriginsLynk services, pricing, workflow boundaries, account ownership, ongoing support, and managed appliance care."
>
  <section class="section-cream page-hero">
    <div class="container container-narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Frequently asked questions</p>
      <h1>Clear answers before you commit.</h1>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-top: var(--space-5)">
        The important distinction is who starts the work, who reviews it, and who remains
        responsible for keeping the system available after launch.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-sunken">
    <div class="container container-narrow">
      <div class="faq-search" role="search">
        <label for="faq-query">Search the FAQ</label>
        <div class="search-control">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10.5" cy="10.5" r="6.5" /><path d="m15.5 15.5 5 5" /></svg>
          <input id="faq-query" type="search" placeholder="Try “monthly fee” or “account access”" autocomplete="off" data-faq-search />
        </div>
        <p class="small muted" id="faq-result-count" aria-live="polite">Showing all {faqs.length} answers.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-list" data-faq-list>
      {faqs.map((faq, index) => (
        <details open={index === 0} data-faq-item data-search={`${faq.question} ${faq.answer}`.toLowerCase()}>
          <summary>{faq.question}</summary>
          <p>{faq.answer}</p>
        </details>
      ))}
      </div>

      <div class="faq-empty" data-faq-empty hidden>
        <h2>No matching answer yet.</h2>
        <p>Try a broader phrase, or tell us what you are trying to solve.</p>
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Request a service</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container container-narrow cta">
      <h2>Still not sure which level fits?</h2>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-top: var(--space-4)">
        Tell us what repeats, how often it happens, and what tools are involved. We will
        recommend a practical first step—including no build when that is the honest answer.
      </p>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Request a service</a>
        <a href="/pricing" class="btn btn-secondary">Compare pricing</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<script is:inline src="/scripts/faq.js" defer></script>

<style>
  .page-hero h1 { max-width: 14ch; }
  .faq-search { margin-bottom: var(--space-6); }
  .faq-search label { display: block; color: var(--ink); font-weight: 680; font-size: var(--text-sm); margin-bottom: var(--space-2); }
  .search-control { position: relative; }
  .search-control svg { position: absolute; left: var(--space-4); top: 50%; transform: translateY(-50%); width: 20px; fill: none; stroke: var(--ink-faint); stroke-width: 1.7; stroke-linecap: round; pointer-events: none; }
  .search-control input { width: 100%; min-height: 52px; padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4) var(--space-3) 3rem; border: 1px solid var(--rule-strong); border-radius: var(--radius); background: var(--ground-raised); }
  .search-control input:focus { outline: none; border-color: var(--accent); box-shadow: 0 0 0 var(--focus-width) var(--accent-ring); }
  #faq-result-count { margin-top: var(--space-2); }
  .faq-list { display: grid; gap: var(--space-3); }

  details {
    background: var(--ground-raised);
    border: var(--border-thin) solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: var(--space-5);
    box-shadow: none;
  }

  details[open] { border-left: var(--border-thick) solid var(--accent); }

  summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--heading-font);
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    font-weight: var(--heading-weight);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
  }

  details p { margin-top: var(--space-4); color: var(--ink-muted); }
  .faq-empty { text-align: center; padding: var(--space-8) var(--space-5); border: 1px dashed var(--rule-strong); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); background: var(--ground-raised); }
  .faq-empty h2 { font-size: var(--text-xl); }
  .faq-empty p { margin: var(--space-3) auto var(--space-5); color: var(--ink-muted); }
  .cta { text-align: center; }
  .cta p { margin-inline: auto; }
  .cta .btn-row { justify-content: center; }
</style>
